Kent Paul Dolan wrote:

> Yes, I recovered a *second* time,
> built myself back to AC -16 by more careful play,
> quickly saved the game [does the recover point get
> moved forward at game save time, I wonder, or is it
> always only at "last entry to level"?].

Recover goes back to the last level entry if the level files (the numbered
ones) are still there. If you save, there's only the save file left, so
recover isn't necessary. If you restart a saved file, the new recover
point is the restart.

Also, note that the game *will* try to perform a panic save if you abort
the game by other means than saving, for example by killing the process
from the ctrl-alt-del screen. This will behave as if you'd Sy-ed.

